<title>HONG KONG: Deutsche Bank ups warrants on H-shares basket.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank ups warrants on H-shares basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG, London Branch, said it is issuing a further 668 million call warrants on a basket of eight locally-listed Chinese enterprises H-shares, on top of an existing 1,038 million warrants  1845.HK which dealings commenced on January 15.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p> Shanghai Petrochemical Co Ltd		 0.25 shares</p>
<p> Anhui Expressway Co Ltd			 0.13 shares</p>
<p> Maanshan Iron and Steel Co Ltd		0.26 shares</p>
<p> Jilin Chemical Industrial Co Ltd	    0.23 shares</p>
<p> Yizheng Chemical Fibre Co Ltd		 0.23 shares</p>
<p>Guangdong Kelon Electrical Holdings Co Ltd 0.05 shares  Guangshen Railway Co Ltd			0.08 shares</p>
<p> Qingling Motors Ltd			     0.07 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.  STRIKE PRICE	HK$2.7826</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.073</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  03.APR.98</p>
<p> LISTING DATE	28.FEB.97</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
